# PetTripFinder Columbus — redirect rules (Netlify `_redirects` format).
# Source of truth (tracked, tested). The assembler copies this to site/_redirects.
# Lines beginning with `#` are comments.
#
# Canonical host is the apex `pettripfinder.com`. `www` redirects ONCE to apex,
# preserving path and query string. There is deliberately:
#   - NO apex -> www redirect (apex stays canonical, no loop);
#   - NO SPA catch-all (e.g. `/*  /index.html  200`) — unknown paths must remain
#     genuine 404s so held/manual-review hotels never resolve;
#   - NO rewrite of existing multipage routes or the /go/ interstitials.
#
# These host rules are DORMANT until the `www` alias is attached to the Netlify
# site in a later, separately authorized stage.

# www -> apex (single hop, forced), path + query preserved via :splat.
https://www.pettripfinder.com/*   https://pettripfinder.com/:splat   301!
http://www.pettripfinder.com/*    https://pettripfinder.com/:splat   301!
